      "side": 1,
      "message": "That is exactly what this change is doing.\n\nGuice does not publish a separate artifact named \"guice-unshaded\". The unshaded variant is published as the same artifact with the `classes` classifier: `com.google.inject:guice:6.0.0:classes`\n\nThe default Guice jar is the fat/shaded one containing the relocated ASM copy. This change switches Gerrit to the `classes` classifier and provides ASM explicitly via Gerrit\u0027s existing OW2 ASM dependency.\n\nMaybe the comment is confusing here because it says \"classes classifier\" without explaining that this is the official unshaded Guice artifact. I can clarify that wording.",
